From c5581e3b9c35abbb60781466b6b4bc4189ce1317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:54:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] cuda: fuse DSV4_HC_POST -> RMS_NORM -> MUL for qwen4exp
 tensor-split prefill

Under -sm tensor each qwen4exp layer ends with the DSV4_HC_POST op (the
unfused hc chain is not correct under the Meta backend), and the next layer
normalizes its output with RMS_NORM + MUL(gamma): two kernels and an extra
read of the hc-wide stream. One kernel now computes the hc_post sum with the
same statements as dsv4_hc_post_f32, stores it (the next residual), and does
the scalar-path reduction, scale and gamma product of rms_norm_f32, so the
output is bit-identical. The graph optimizer keeps x / residual / post alive
until the MUL (other blocks still read them while xn is written); an overlap
check falls back to the unfused kernels. GGML_CUDA_HC_POST_RMS=0 turns it off.

2x R9700, -sm tensor: half-depth Flash-Next llama-bench pp31744 6294 ->
6705 t/s; server prefill 31.5k 6508 -> 6932, 159k 5632 -> 5958, greedy hash
unchanged; full model 31.5k 3008 -> 3196, 159k 2682 -> 2829, 259.6k 2436 ->
2552, greedy / pwid / seeded hashes unchanged; full-logit KLD vs the unfused
kernels equal to the base-vs-base control at 8k and 32k.
